   "subject": "Re: labling tips",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I could solve the issue using the phylobase package.</div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\">library(phylobase)</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\">tr2 &lt;- phylo4d(aa.tree, df)</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\">p = ggtree::ggtree(tr2)</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\">p = p + geom_tiplab(size=3,  align=TRUE, aes(label = label2), hjust= 0) </span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\">pp = gheatmap(p, fc.mat, offset = 1.2, width=0.5,</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\">              color = &quot;white&quot;, colnames_angle = 45, colnames_offset_y = -1)</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\">p1 = pp + scale_fill_gradient(low = &quot;black&quot;, high = &quot;red&quot;, </span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\">            na.value = &quot;white&quot;, trans = &quot;log&quot;, breaks=c(0.001,0.01, 0.1, 1,10))</span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,153,0)\"><br></span></div><br>On Thursday, February 16, 2017 at 6:13:34 PM UTC+1, Dana Winther wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Basically, I am following the recommendation given at <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/ggtree/faq/#modify-tip-labels\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/ggtree/faq/%23modify-tip-labels&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482794884000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1T75Y23vQMD4MWVaYYKObY\">here</a> </div><div><br></div><div>By default I can plot my tree as following </div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,229,153)\"><br></span></div><div><div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,229,153)\">aa.tree = phy_tree(aa)</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,229,153)\">p = ggtree::ggtree(aa.tree) </span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,229,153)\">p = p + geom_tiplab(size=3,  align=TRUE)</span></div></div><div><br></div><div>however, I would like to have other labels, therefore, I made a dataframe as </div><div><div><div><br><span style=\"background-color:rgb(182,215,168)\">df = data.frame(label = as.character(tax_table(aa)[,&quot;Row.names&quot;]), </span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(182,215,168)\">                label2 = as.character(tax_table(aa)[,&quot;final.tax.2print&quot;]))</span></div></div></div><div><br></div><div>which looks like </div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.8667px;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(255,255,255);background-color:rgb(15,15,15);white-space:pre-wrap!important\">  label                    label2\r\n1  x_12 x_12 o__Clostridiales/f_?\r\n2  x_37         x_37 f__S24-7/g_?\r\n3  x_40 x_40 g__Lactobacillus/s_?\r\n4  x_47         x_47 f__S24-7/g_?\r\n5  x_52 x_52 o__Bacteroidales/f_?\r\n6  x_54 x_54 o__Clostridiales/f_?</pre></div><div><br></div><div>where the first column is the original labels and the second column is the one I wish to display,</div><div><br></div><div>and eventually use</div><div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(182,215,168)\">aa.tree = phy_tree(aa)</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(182,215,168)\">p = ggtree::ggtree(aa.tree) </span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(182,215,168)\">p = p + geom_tiplab(size=3,  align=TRUE) %&lt;+% df + geom_tiplab(aes(label=label2))</span></div></div></div><div><br></div><div>but I get the following error</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.8667px;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(255,255,255);background-color:rgb(15,15,15);white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,153,153)\">Error in <a href=\"http://fix.by\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://fix.by&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482794884000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1GCd92J35kupacYikpenXW\">fix.by</a>(by.x, x) : &#39;by&#39; must specify a uniquely valid column\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,153,153)\">In addition: </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,153,153)\">Warning message:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,153,153)\">The plyr::rename operation has created duplicates for the following name(s): (`size`) </span></pre><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.8667px;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(255,255,255);background-color:rgb(15,15,15);white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,153,153)\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">I wonder what I am doing wrong ! </div><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Thanks,</div></span></pre></div></div></blockquote></div>"
